NAME "How /config displays a stored agentMode of auto"
WINDOW 100 34
TARGET both
SETTINGS '{"agentMode":"auto","showTips":false}'

# Scene 56 opened the Agent Mode submenu with no mode stored, and the two
# panes disagreed on the *list*:
#
#     agy      default (current) / accept-edits / plan           (3 rows)
#     pigasus  default (current) / accept-edits / auto / plan    (4 rows)
#
# Before treating that as a defect, the other direction has to be measured:
# a session whose stored mode IS "auto". If agy folds auto onto default — the
# row reads "default (current)" — then "auto" is not a value the reference
# offers and pigasus's fourth row is an invention. If agy instead names auto
# as current, the extra row is legitimate and only the ordering differs.
#
# The composer row is in the same snapshot, and it is the row that settles
# the question. A bare ">" in agy is NOT evidence that auto has no banner:
#
#   agy Agent Mode row here reads "default" even though settings.json stores
#   "agentMode": "auto". The binary declines to enter auto — its string table
#   says why: "Auto mode is not available: it needs the OS terminal sandbox
#   and may not be rolled out to you yet" — and falls back to default. The
#   bare prompt is the default mode's prompt.
#
# The auto banner string is present verbatim in agy 1.5.18:
#   "Auto mode: edits & safe commands auto-approved (shift+tab to cycle)"
# so the reference does name auto in the composer. Do not infer the banner
# from a capture on a host whose terminal sandbox is unavailable; check the
# Agent Mode row first, which is what this snapshot photographs.

BOOT_BOTH
WAIT_READY 15s
SLEEP 1200ms
SNAPSHOT "01_boot_auto"

TYPE "/config"
ENTER
WAIT_TEXT "Color Scheme" 20s
SLEEP 600ms
SNAPSHOT "02_config_agent_mode_row"

DIFF
CLEANUP
